      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115135,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9240/3 Mesenchymal chondrosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115136,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B50.Z &amp; XH8X47 Chondrosarcoma of bone and articular cartilage of unspecified sites &amp; Mesenchymal chondrosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115137,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115138,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115139,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common sites in the head and neck are the jaws (the mandible more frequently), followed by the skull {3697943; 6825046; 6861090; 15233236; 17681487; 29582189}. Within the sinonasal tract, the maxillary sinus is most commonly affected, followed by the ethmoid and nasal cavity {12792311}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115140,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with swelling, pain, and possible pathological fracture.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>An aggressive lytic and destructive mass is seen radiologically, sometimes with soft tissue extension and calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115141,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p >MCSs account for 2&ndash;10% of all chondrosarcomas, and 20&ndash;30% of cases arise in the head and neck {14416919}. The peak incidence is in the third decade of life (age range: 7&ndash;80&nbsp;years) {10813732}. There is no sex predilection {25529371; 26975384}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-13T09:24:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115142,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115143,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Almost all cases harbour a specific <em>HEY1</em>::<em>NCOA2</em> fusion gene, or (much more rarely) <em>IRF2BP2</em>::<em>CDX1</em>. Small-cell areas show <em>TP53</em> loss, RB1 pathway alterations, and homozygous loss of <em>CDKN2A</em> {22674453; 23415961}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115144,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MCS is a grey, grey-white, or pink tumour and can be soft, firm, or hard with nodules of cartilage and bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115145,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>MCS has a characteristic biphasic pattern. Large areas are composed of small, uniform, round to spindle-shaped cells, which resemble those of Ewing sarcoma, often with a perivascular arrangement and haemangiopericytoma-like pattern, necrosis, and frequent mitoses. Admixed lobules of highly differentiated cartilage may be limited or extensive and can exhibit calcification and immature ossification.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry shows positivity for membranous CD99 and nuclear SOX9. NKX3-1 {31972596} has been suggested to be highly specific; there may be aberrant muscle marker expression.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-13T09:24:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115146,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytology shows small cells with high N:C&nbsp;ratios, singly and in clumps, in a basophilic extracellular matrix.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115147,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>HEY1</em>::<em>NCOA2</em> recurrent translocation is present in almost all MCSs {22034177; 23252872}; <em>IRF2BP2</em>::<em>CDX1</em> is reported much more rarely {23185413}. <em>IDH1</em> and <em>IDH2</em> mutations do not occur {21598255; 24680178}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:10:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115148,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a sarcoma with a prominent primitive component of round to spindled cells punctated with islands of mature cartilage.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>HEY1</em>::<em>NCOA2</em> fusion (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-13T09:25:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115149,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p >Staging follows the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-13T09:25:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115150,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 177,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "<p>MCS has a high local recurrence rate, with metastasis potentially occurring after a long disease-free interval. MCS in general has 5- and 10-year survival rates of 51% and 43% respectively, depending on the site, surgical resectability, and the type and duration of therapy {26975384}. Jaw tumours generally have a better prognosis {6402853; 6825046; 13883114}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-12-19T14:27:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]